From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:39:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bd_read_ext(): tell a new play item before the bytes of its
 clip

When a read reached the end of a play item, _bd_read() opened the clip of
the next one and went on reading it in the same call: the read returned
the first bytes of the new clip together with its BD_EVENT_PLAYITEM (and
BD_EVENT_DISCONTINUITY). A player that opens its demuxer again for a new
play item (Kodi with the disc's menus does, unless the join is seamless
and keeps its streams) gave those bytes to the demuxer of the play item
before. The new demuxer then started up to an aligned unit (6144 bytes)
into the clip, inside the PES packet of its first random-access picture,
and the video of the new play item began only at its next random-access
picture; the old demuxer got the cut first picture of the new clip at its
end.

With the event queue (bd_read_ext()), the read that opens the clip of the
next play item now returns nothing, with the events, and the bytes of the
clip come from the next read on. The bytes and their order are the same,
only how they are split across reads differs; bd_read() is unchanged. A
seamless angle change is left as it is: only bd_seamless_angle_change()
starts one, and nothing in LibreELEC Hades calls it.

Telling the play item before its bytes is CroqueMr's idea
(libreelec-x86-DV, 0002-navigation-read-boundary.patch). Written anew for
LibreELEC Hades.
---
 src/libbluray/bluray.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libbluray/bluray.c b/src/libbluray/bluray.c
index bc2a258..817430b 100644
--- a/src/libbluray/bluray.c
+++ b/src/libbluray/bluray.c
@@ -2499,7 +2499,16 @@ static int64_t _clip_seek_time(BLURAY *bd, uint32_t tick)
     return bd->s_pos;
 }
 
-static int _bd_read(BLURAY *bd, unsigned char *buf, int len)
+/*
+ * announce: the caller reads with the event queue (bd_read_ext()). A read that reaches the end of
+ * a play item opens the clip of the next one and returns nothing: its events (BD_EVENT_PLAYITEM,
+ * and BD_EVENT_DISCONTINUITY when it does not join seamlessly) come with that read, and its bytes
+ * from the next read on. A player that opens its demuxer again for a new play item then gives
+ * each demuxer the bytes of its own play item; when the events came with the first bytes of the
+ * new clip, those went to the demuxer of the play item before.
+ * (A seamless angle change, which only bd_seamless_angle_change() starts, is left as it was.)
+ */
+static int _bd_read(BLURAY *bd, unsigned char *buf, int len, int announce)
 {
     BD_STREAM *st = &bd->st0;
     int out_len = 0;
@@ -2581,6 +2590,9 @@ static int _bd_read(BLURAY *bd, unsigned char *buf, int len)
                         _queue_event(bd, BD_EVENT_DISCONTINUITY, st->clip->in_time);
                     }
 
+                    if (announce) {
+                        return 0;
+                    }
                 }
 
                 int r = _read_block(bd, st, bd->int_buf);
@@ -2650,7 +2662,7 @@ static int _bd_read(BLURAY *bd, unsigned char *buf, int len)
         return out_len;
 }
 
-static int _bd_read_locked(BLURAY *bd, unsigned char *buf, int len)
+static int _bd_read_locked(BLURAY *bd, unsigned char *buf, int len, int announce)
 {
     BD_STREAM *st = &bd->st0;
     int r;
@@ -2670,7 +2682,7 @@ static int _bd_read_locked(BLURAY *bd, unsigned char *buf, int len)
 
     BD_DEBUG(DBG_STREAM, "Reading [%d bytes] at %" PRIu64 "...\n", len, bd->s_pos);
 
-    r = _bd_read(bd, buf, len);
+    r = _bd_read(bd, buf, len, announce);
 
     /* mark tracking */
     if (bd->next_mark >= 0 && bd->s_pos > bd->next_mark_pos) {
@@ -2691,7 +2703,7 @@ int bd_read(BLURAY *bd, unsigned char *buf, int len)
     int result;
 
     bd_mutex_lock(&bd->mutex);
-    result = _bd_read_locked(bd, buf, len);
+    result = _bd_read_locked(bd, buf, len, 0);
     bd_mutex_unlock(&bd->mutex);
 
     return result;
@@ -4495,7 +4507,8 @@ static int _read_ext(BLURAY *bd, unsigned char *buf, int len, BD_EVENT *event)
         }
     }
 
-    int bytes = _bd_read_locked(bd, buf, len);
+    /* with the event queue, a change of clip is told before the bytes of the new clip */
+    int bytes = _bd_read_locked(bd, buf, len, bd->event_queue != NULL);
 
     if (bytes == 0) {
 
